<section id="welcome" class="alt"><div class="wrap intro">
<h2>Find support, healing, and hope</h2>
<div><p>If you’re struggling with anxiety, depression, trauma, stress, relationship challenges, or a major life transition, you don’t have to face it alone.</p>
<p>A New Perspective Therapy PLLC offers evidence-based, trauma-informed therapy for adolescents and adults in Swansboro, Jacksonville, Camp Lejeune, Morehead City, and across North Carolina by secure telehealth. Every treatment plan is tailored to you, to build healthier coping skills, resilience, and lasting change.</p>
<p>This practice celebrates diversity and embraces inclusivity.</p></div>
</div></section>

<div class="band"><div class="wrap"><p>Informed, compassionate care for military members, veterans, and their families, with specialized military behavioral health training.</p></div></div>

<section id="services"><div class="wrap">
<div class="head"><h2>Therapy services</h2><p>Like clothing, therapy is not one size fits all. Reach out for a personalized approach.</p></div>
<div class="svc">
<article><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#sprig"/></svg><h3>Individual therapy</h3><p>One-to-one individualized sessions in a confidential setting, in person or virtual.</p></article>
<article><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#sprig"/></svg><h3>Walk and talk</h3><p>Steps to healing in nature, for those who prefer a relaxed, outdoor session.</p></article>
<article><svg aria-hidden="true"><use href="#sprig"/></svg><h3>EMDR</h3><p>Trauma-focused therapy to reprocess distressing memories and experiences, easing symptoms and promoting healing.</p></article>
</div>
<ul class="when" aria-label="Therapy may help when">
<li><b>You want mental health support.</b> A safe space to explore anxiety, depression, or trauma.</li>
<li><b>You’re feeling stressed.</b> Strategies and coping tools for your stressors.</li>
<li><b>You want stronger relationships</b> with a partner, family, friends, or colleagues.</li>
<li><b>You want to explore who you are,</b> with room for self-reflection.</li>
<li><b>Life is changing:</b> career shifts, military relocation, new parenting roles, or an empty nest.</li>
<li><b>Grief and loss,</b> including the loss of a pet.</li>
<li><b>You want new skills:</b> goals, communication, self-esteem, and positive lifestyle changes.</li>
</ul></div></section>

<section id="walk" class="walk"><div class="wrap">
<div><h2>Steps to healing in nature</h2>
<p style="margin-top:1.2rem">Individual sessions are offered in person or as nature-based walk-and-talk sessions in:</p>
<ul class="towns"><li>Swansboro</li><li>Jacksonville</li><li>Cedar Point</li><li>Cape Carteret</li><li>Morehead City</li><li>Emerald Isle</li></ul>
<p style="margin-top:1.4rem">Virtual sessions are available throughout North Carolina.</p></div>
<div class="path" role="img" aria-label="Placeholder for a coastal walking-trail photo"><svg viewBox="0 0 400 500" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#branch"/></svg><img class="pic" src="images/walk.jpg" alt="A walk-and-talk setting" onload="this.parentNode.classList.add('has')" onerror="this.remove()"><span class="ph">Photo: walk-and-talk setting</span></div>
</div></section>

<section id="about" class="alt"><div class="wrap about">
<div><div class="portrait" role="img" aria-label="Placeholder for a portrait of the therapist"><svg class="leafy" aria-hidden="true"><use href="#branch"/></svg><img class="pic" src="images/portrait.jpg" alt="Lisa Fitzpatrick, LCSWA" onload="this.parentNode.classList.add('has')" onerror="this.remove()"><span class="ph">Portrait goes here</span></div>
<p class="dog">Pictured on the current site: Cora, therapy dog in training.</p></div>
<div><h2>Hello, I’m glad you’re here.</h2>
<p style="margin-top:1.4rem">Life has a way of piling things on: relationships, work stress, transitions, losses, or moments when you just don’t feel like yourself. Therapy can be a supportive, judgment-free space where you don’t have to have everything figured out.</p>
<p>Building trust and connection is at the heart of my work. I want you to feel heard, respected, and supported from the very first session. Whenever you’re ready, I’m here to walk alongside you.</p>
<p><strong>Lisa Fitzpatrick, LCSWA</strong><br>A New Perspective Therapy PLLC</p></div>
</div></section>

<section id="expect"><div class="wrap">
<div class="head"><h2>Getting started</h2><p>Reaching out may be the most difficult part of therapy, but the rewards may be just what you’ve been seeking.</p></div>
<ol class="steps">
<li><h3>Book a free consultation</h3><p>A free, no-obligation 15-minute call to see whether we’re a good fit.</p></li>
<li><h3>Begin with an assessment</h3><p>Your first session is a 55-minute initial assessment, in person, on a walk, or by telehealth.</p></li>
<li><h3>Continue at your pace</h3><p>Ongoing 55-minute sessions, tailored to your needs and goals.</p></li>
</ol></div></section>

